        {
          "kind": "branch",
          "title": "1.5 — How to Approach a System Design Problem",
          "hLevel": 1,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "summary",
              "title": "Whether it's an interview or a real project, follow this framework",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Step 1: Clarify Requirements (3–5 minutes)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Never jump into designing. Ask questions first.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Example — You're asked: \"Design a URL shortener\"",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Good clarifying questions",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "How many URLs will be shortened per day? (100M)",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "How many redirects per day? (10",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "Should shortened URLs expire? (Yes, configurable)",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "Do we need analytics (click count, geo, device)? (Yes)",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "What's the expected latency for a redirect? (<100ms)",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Step 2: Estimate Scale (2–3 minutes)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Step 3: High-Level Design (10 minutes)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Sketch the major components and how they connect.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Diagram showing Client, API Gateway, URL Service, Database, Redis Cache",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Step 4: Deep Dive (15–20 minutes)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Pick 2–3 components and go deep.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Step 5: Address Bottlenecks & Edge Cases (5 minutes)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "What if the database goes down?",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "What if one URL gets 1 million clicks/minute (viral)?",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "leaf",
                  "title": "How do you prevent abuse?",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "branch",
          "title": "1.7 — Design Choices: Your First Architecture",
          "hLevel": 1,
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "summary",
              "title": "Here's a decision framework for choosing your starting architecture based on your current scale and team.",
              "hLevel": 5,
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Decision: Monolith vs Microservices from Day 1?",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Diagram showing Start with Monolith, Microservices, Modular Monolith, 10 engineers, 10-50 engineers",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Table summarizing Factor, Monolith, Modular Monolith, Microservices for Best for, Deploy speed, Complexity, Scaling",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "The key insight: Almost every successful company started with a monolith and broke it apart later.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Decision: SQL vs NoSQL (First Pass)",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "You'll go deep in Module 5 (Databases), but here's the first-pass heuristic",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Diagram showing SQL Database, Document Store, Key-Value Store, Graph Database, Structured, relational (users, orders, payments",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "When in doubt, start with PostgreSQL.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "sub",
              "title": "Decision: Consistency vs Availability",
              "hLevel": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "This is the fundamental trade-off in distributed systems (you'll explore this deeply in Phase 4 with the CAP Theorem).",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Diagram showing Strong Consistency, Every read returns, Examples, Eventual Consistency, Reads may return",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "summary",
                  "title": "Rule of thumb: If showing stale data costs money or trust (payments, inventory), choose strong consistency.",
                  "hLevel": 5,
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
